---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/prose.css';
import { SITE, url } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What ForkLore is and who writes it.">
  <article class="wrap page">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        ForkLore is an independent tech blog exploring cybersecurity, AI vulnerabilities, blockchain
        cryptography, digital forensics and the hidden mechanics of online systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's a comic-style tech blog on purpose. Security advisories, protocol specs and cryptography papers
        can be dry, so ForkLore tries to keep the boring parts fun: bold headings, plain language and a bit of
        personality, without dumbing down the technical detail.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name is a fork in two senses: the code you clone to see how something really works, and the
        folklore that grows up around technology when nobody checks. Posts here try to separate the two.
      </p>
      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <p>
        I'm {SITE.author}, a Master of Cybersecurity student at RMIT. I write up what I learn from labs,
        CTFs, coursework and my own projects. Everything tested here is tested on systems I own or am
        authorised to test.
      </p>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Find me on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>, follow along with the <a href={url("/rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a>, or
        <a href={SITE.coffee}>buy me a coffee</a> if a post saved you some time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .page { padding-top: 48px; max-width: calc(68ch + 2 * var(--gutter)); }
  .page-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.5vw, 3.4rem); letter-spacing: 0.005em; margin-bottom: 28px; }
</style>
